<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Database>
    <EnglishText>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MOD_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_NAME">
            <Text>Zoom, Tilt, &amp; Rotate</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_MOD_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Zoom closer and farther than the game allows, tip the camera between looking straight down and looking toward the horizon, and turn the view to face any direction.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_OPTIONS_GROUP_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE">
            <Text>Zoom, Tilt, &amp; Rotate</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_CLOSE_UP">
            <Text>How close you can zoom in</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_CLOSE_UP_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>How far the six extra notches take you past the game's closest view, which counts as 1x. At 7x you see a unit up close. At 18x a unit fills the screen. At 36x, the most the game's camera allows, you'll see a single sword blade and the ground goes soft. Changes apply right away.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_CLOSE_UP_CLOSER">
            <Text>Closer (7x)</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_CLOSE_UP_MUCH_CLOSER">
            <Text>Much closer (18x)</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_CLOSE_UP_ALL_THE_WAY">
            <Text>All the way (36x)</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_KEEP_ANGLE">
            <Text>Keep the angle when zoomed far out</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_KEEP_ANGLE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Zooming out past the game's farthest view turns the camera to look straight down. Tick this to keep your angle instead. The camera only tips down as far as it needs to keep the sky off the screen, and at the game's own angle it doesn't tip at all. Changes apply right away.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DEGREES">
            <Text>{1_Num}°</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_TURN_STEP">
            <Text>Turn step</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_TURN_STEP_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>How far one press of a turn key, or the turn buttons in the camera panel, turns the view. The view stays facing that way until you turn it again or go back to normal.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_ANGLE_STEP">
            <Text>Angle step</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_ANGLE_STEP_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>How far one press of an angle key, or the angle buttons in the camera panel, tips the camera between looking straight down and looking toward the horizon.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_SHOW_DIALS">
            <Text>Show the camera dials on screen</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_SHOW_DIALS_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Keeps a small zoom gauge, compass and angle gauge at the top left, under the victories and the journal, on a see-through backing. Drag along the zoom gauge to zoom, around the compass to turn the view, and along the angle gauge to tip it. They step aside while a screen or popup is open.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DIAL_ZOOM">
            <Text>Zoom gauge on screen</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DIAL_ZOOM_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Shows the zoom gauge among the dials on screen. Drag along it to zoom.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DIAL_COMPASS">
            <Text>Compass on screen</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DIAL_COMPASS_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Shows the compass among the dials on screen. Drag around it to turn the view.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DIAL_ANGLE">
            <Text>Angle gauge on screen</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_DIAL_ANGLE_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>Shows the angle gauge among the dials on screen. Drag along it to tip the camera.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_KEYS">
            <Text>Camera keys</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_KEYS_DESCRIPTION">
            <Text>The keys that tip the camera, turn the view, go back to normal and open the camera panel. Out of the box they're Shift with the arrow keys, 0 and C.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_OPTION_KEYS_OPEN">
            <Text>Change keys</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_TITLE">
            <Text>Camera keys</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_INTRO">
            <Text>Press Change, then the keys you want, holding any of Ctrl, Alt (Option on a Mac) and Shift with them. Esc stops waiting.</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_CHANGE">
            <Text>Change</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_CLEAR">
            <Text>Clear</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_RESET">
            <Text>Reset keys</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_WAITING">
            <Text>Press the keys…</Text>
        </Row>
        <Row Tag="LOC_ZOOM_TILT_ROTATE_KEYS_NONE">
            <Text>None</Text>
        </Row>
